 3. 🦾 Claude helping build its next version 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Chart: Anthropic Claude is helping Anthropic develop the next, more intelligent version of itself, the AI lab announced :

 "Claude is not operating fully autonomously for any measured subset of AI R&amp;D work," Anthropic said. "Claude 'leads' 26% of Anthropic's AI R&amp;D work." Why it matters: The announcement was unclear about how close the company believes it is to achieving recursive self-improvement ( RSI , when AI builds itself). But the pace at which Claude is increasingly contributing to research and development is escalating, AP notes : 

 The portion of work Claude "leads," or does in large part while remaining under human supervision, was zero in February. Six months later, in August, it was 26%. Read the announcement . 

 
 
