 4. 🤷 Stumping Wall Street 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep. Chart: Axios/Emily Peck JPMorgan analysts offered an unusually blunt assessment of the oil market: They have no idea what happens next.

 "For the first time since the start of the Iran conflict, we don't have a baseline view. We simply don't know how to model the endgame." Why it matters: Market watchers have come to grips with the likelihood that the status of the Strait of Hormuz — and the number of barrels getting through — will be messy for months to come, Axios' Ben Geman writes. 

 Go deeper with Axios Future of Energy . 
 
