 6. 🇻🇪 Scoop: Trump plans Venezuela sit-down 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump hosted a dinner for 100+ hunters and fishermen in the Rose Garden last night. Photo: Alex Brandon/AP President Trump is planning a first-ever meeting with Venezuela's interim president, Delcy Rodríguez, as early as Tuesday, sources familiar with the discussions tell Axios' Marc Caputo. 

 Why it matters: The potential meeting showcases the close relations between the nations under Trump. But it's also fraught with political risks that stretch from Miami to Caracas. 👀 Behind the scenes: Trump is already planning to meet with Gulf leaders at the UN General Assembly in New York next week to discuss the Iran war, and those who know his thinking say he wants to make time for a sideline sit-down with Rodríguez, sources said.

 A Trump adviser told Axios: "Iran is tough, but Venezuela is without a doubt the president's top success and Delcy is a key to that. Unless something goes really wrong, the president wants to make time." A senior administration official cautioned: "Nothing is finalized. This is up to the president." Share this story . 

 
 
