 8. 🍌 1 fun thing: Parties go bananas 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Attendees at the "eat an apple with me" event in D.C. last month. Photo: Tierney L. Cross for The Washington Post via Getty Images Young people are showing up by the hundreds for parties built around absurdly niche premises, Axios D.C.'s Mimi Montgomery writes. 

 There's a party happening this weekend in D.C. that's BYOB — Bring Your Own Banana. A recent " eat an apple with me " party drew hundreds out to Washington's Meridian Hill Park. Other greatest hits include a " Smoke a Cigarette With Me " party that brought 1,500 people together to rip cigs in New York's Washington Square Park. Hundreds gathered to watch a dude in Philly eat a rotisserie chicken . Why it matters: The premise is almost beside the point. It's a low-stakes excuse to hang out in real life at a time when loneliness is widespread and young people are drinking less.

